  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A company called Exodus Propulsion has built a device that gets lighter on a scale when it is switched on and heavier when it is flipped over. That is the claim of Charles Buhler, a scientist the episode bills as a NASA chief, who says he took part in the work: \"we put stuff on a scale and we turn it on, it gets lighter,\" he tells Michels, adding that the results are \"going through a peer review\" and that a second patent application has been filed and is being looked at by patent examiners. If true, it would be a push with no fuel thrown out the back, a kind of working antigravity."
